    "narrativeText": "Montverd FC's debut season in the Premier League was nothing short of historic — Pep Guardiola's side claimed the title with 95 points and 92 goals, with Florian Wirtz posting an extraordinary 36-goal campaign from the CAM role in his very first year at the club. In Europe, Montverd were the most dominant team in the UCL league phase (1st place, 36 GF / 6 GA across 8 matches) and swept through Athletic Club and RB Leipzig with a combined 26–3 aggregate before running into eventual champions Real Madrid in the semi-final, losing a hard-fought tie 8–4 on aggregate. The Carabao Cup was claimed emphatically with a 4–0 demolition of Liverpool in the final — a statement of intent that this squad's ceiling remains untouched.",
